<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n34336" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pĕdĭca</span></b> , ae,
			f.
		pes, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a
				shackle</i>, <i>fetter</i>, or <i>chain for the feet</i>, <i>a springe</i>, <i>gin</i>, <i>snare</i> (cf.: compes,
			vinculum tendicula). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>, <i><span class="en">Plaut.
				Poen. 3, 1, 10</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Liv. 21, 36</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tunc gruibus pedicas et retia ponere cervis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					G. 1, 307</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 15, 473</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Vulg. Jer. 5,
				26</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quid, si pedes pedicis coartentur?</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">App. Flor. p. 357, 29</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, of the spider's web, <i><span class="en">Plin. 11,
				24, 28, § 81</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>, <i>a shackle</i>, <i>fetter</i> (post-class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">amoris,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">App. M. 2, p. 116, 40</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nuptiales,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 6</span></i>
			, p. 182, 41.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
